{
  "dom_id": "step-q180226",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "If $0.6y=-4.8$, then $y=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $10$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.6y & =-4.8 \\\\ 10\\cdot (0.6y) & =10\\cdot (-4.8) \\\\ 6y & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y & =-48 \\\\ \\frac{6y}{6} & =\\frac{-48}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{6}y}{\\cancel{6}} & =-8 \\\\ y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
